Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: a stub's guest write in one copy when the range is one piece of host memory

writeGuestBytes (the stubs' helper) looked every byte up on its own: sceVu0UnitMatrix's 64 bytes, called from the
game's matrix set-up many times a frame, cost ~0.8% of Deep Amazon's game thread. When the first and the last byte
are one piece of host memory (main RAM, the scratchpad) the range is copied at once; the same bytes are written.

ps2xRuntime:
- Stubs/Helpers/Support.h: writeGuestBytes, the contiguous case first.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Helpers/Support.h b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Helpers/Support.h
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Helpers/Support.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Helpers/Support.h
@@ -676,6 +676,19 @@
             return true;
         }
 
+        // The whole range at once when its first and last bytes are one piece of host memory (main RAM, the
+        // scratchpad): the byte-by-byte lookups below cost sceVu0UnitMatrix's 64 bytes ~0.8% of a busy game thread.
+        if (len - 1u <= 0xFFFFFFFFull - addr)
+        {
+            uint8_t *first = getMemPtr(rdram, addr);
+            uint8_t *last = getMemPtr(rdram, static_cast<uint32_t>(addr + (len - 1u)));
+            if (first && last && last - first == static_cast<std::ptrdiff_t>(len - 1u))
+            {
+                std::memcpy(first, src, len);
+                return true;
+            }
+        }
+
         bool allViaPtrs = true;
         for (size_t i = 0; i < len; ++i)
         {
